MAYVILLE - All the members of a committee that helps planting trees in the village have resigned, apparently because of how the village board operates.

Laura Marsala, who had been the Mayville Tree Advisory Committee chairperson, sent a letter to the Mayville Village Board announcing her resignation.

"It's with regret that I am announcing, effective today (Oct. 13), that the Mayville Tree Advisory Committee is stepping back until conditions are more conducive to accomplish our goals. We have waited three years for a formal tree board to be written into law, and it's time to put our energy into projects that can be completed," she said in a letter that was sent to the village board.

In the letter, Marsala noted the members have a lot of experience.

"I would like the public to know what we feel is a lost opportunity and the impact this decision has on our community in the way of free services:

• Loss of volunteer hours, knowledge, and experience of a certified arborist;

• Of a high school field and environmental sciences teacher;

• Loss of volunteer hours of 7 other enthusiastic individuals who were willing to do the hard work;
